WEBVTT

00:01.534 --> 00:04.670
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.672 --> 00:07.806
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:07.808 --> 00:11.510
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.512 --> 00:14.513
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.515 --> 00:17.883
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.885 --> 00:21.286
♪ lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.288 --> 00:22.688
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:22.690 --> 00:24.156
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.158 --> 00:30.562
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.202 --> 00:37.236
Tv announcer:
We now return to jeremy piven

00:37.238 --> 00:39.171
<i>As the incredible hulk.</i>

00:39.173 --> 00:40.873
You wouldn't like me
when I'm angry.

00:40.875 --> 00:42.574
I don't like you now.

00:42.576 --> 00:44.543
Brian, I need the tv.

00:44.545 --> 00:45.911
Why is rupert
wearing a top hat?

00:45.913 --> 00:48.213
Because, brian,
tonight we sup on

00:48.215 --> 00:49.848
The finest feast of
the television season.

00:49.850 --> 00:51.550
It is the
season finale

00:51.552 --> 00:53.085
<i>Of the cadwalliders
of essex.</i>

00:53.087 --> 00:55.220
<i>The what?
The cadwalliders
of essex.</i>

00:55.222 --> 00:56.555
It's groundbreaking.

00:56.557 --> 00:58.557
It's a british show
about a wealthy family

00:58.559 --> 00:59.691
Dealing with
slight change.

00:59.693 --> 01:01.326
Oh, I thought
that got cancelled.

01:01.328 --> 01:03.062
<i>No, that was the caduggans
of aubrey muse.</i>

01:03.064 --> 01:05.330
Is that the one where even
the children have muttonchops?

01:05.332 --> 01:07.232
<i>No, that's the whittakers
of edgerton crescent.</i>

01:07.234 --> 01:08.734
All these shows
sound the same.

01:08.736 --> 01:09.535
Who's in this one?

01:09.537 --> 01:10.736
Penelope
westworth-harrington.

01:10.738 --> 01:11.870
Who's that?

01:11.872 --> 01:14.440
Penelope westworth-harrington?
Oh, come on!

01:14.442 --> 01:16.208
<i>From the roysters of
pumbridge on thames?</i>

01:16.210 --> 01:18.444
Her uncle was steward
to the queen's privy!

01:18.446 --> 01:22.247
<i>She got plowed on a pile
of hay in game of thrones.</i>

01:22.249 --> 01:23.582
Oh, yeah. Yeah.

01:23.584 --> 01:24.616
She's hot.

01:24.618 --> 01:26.251
Ugh, you're an idiot.

01:26.253 --> 01:27.886
Like a guy who cheats
on his right hand

01:27.888 --> 01:29.421
With his left hand.

01:29.423 --> 01:30.722
I want to stay,

01:30.724 --> 01:32.858
But I just got called
back into the office.

01:32.860 --> 01:34.460
What do you want from me?

01:34.462 --> 01:35.561
I'm sorry, all right?

01:35.563 --> 01:36.728
Just get off my back!

01:36.730 --> 01:38.530
I'm out of here.

01:40.266 --> 01:41.934
God, it took me forever
to get awa...

01:41.936 --> 01:42.968
(gunshot)

01:42.970 --> 01:43.969
Oh, my god!

01:43.971 --> 01:45.270
No!

01:45.272 --> 01:47.372
What have you done?!

01:47.374 --> 01:48.574
Wait! Stop!

01:48.576 --> 01:49.708
No, please!

01:49.710 --> 01:50.709
I'm begging you!

01:50.711 --> 01:52.478
(gunshot)

01:54.814 --> 01:56.882
(sobbing)

02:02.388 --> 02:03.589
(classical music playing
over tv)

02:03.591 --> 02:04.756
Oh, it's starting!

02:04.758 --> 02:06.391
I'm gonna live-tweet the show

02:06.393 --> 02:08.794
And ruin it for everyone
in other time zones.

02:13.133 --> 02:16.902
I would like to learn
to bathe myself.

02:20.106 --> 02:23.075
Everything I've ever
heard is vexing.

02:23.077 --> 02:24.443
Oh! Oh!

02:24.445 --> 02:26.778
This is the fastest-moving
episode I've ever seen!

02:26.780 --> 02:27.746
Wouldn't it be marvelous

02:27.748 --> 02:29.815
To be a part of
a family like that?

02:29.817 --> 02:31.650
Ah-ha, I found
that chick in the hay.

02:31.652 --> 02:33.619
Peter and chris (chanting):
Unga bunga, unga bunga,

02:33.621 --> 02:34.820
Unga bunga.

02:34.822 --> 02:36.622
What is that?
What's happening?

02:36.624 --> 02:39.858
Unga bunga, unga bunga,
unga bunga.

02:39.860 --> 02:40.926
Peter, what are you doing?

02:40.928 --> 02:42.127
Playing unga bunga.

02:42.129 --> 02:43.128
It's the championship.

02:43.130 --> 02:44.496
Go away!

02:44.498 --> 02:46.765
This is why zillow estimates
our house at $4.00.

02:46.767 --> 02:48.200
What the hell is unga bunga?

02:48.202 --> 02:49.635
Two guys run
at each other

02:49.637 --> 02:51.703
With mattresses,
and, um...

02:51.705 --> 02:53.272
Th-that's kind of it.

02:53.274 --> 02:55.507
Stop explaining it to the dog!

02:55.509 --> 02:56.775
Let's do this!

02:56.777 --> 02:59.311
(yelling wildly)

02:59.313 --> 03:01.446
Stop it!
I'm trying to watch my program!

03:01.448 --> 03:02.814
Whoa, chris, look!
Mom's naked!

03:02.816 --> 03:03.882
Where?

03:03.884 --> 03:04.950
You creep.

03:06.819 --> 03:08.620
(gasps)
no!

03:08.622 --> 03:10.556
Peter, what's going on in...

03:10.558 --> 03:11.557
Unga bunga!
(crashing)

03:11.559 --> 03:13.859
You... You imbeciles!

03:13.861 --> 03:14.893
You ruined my night!

03:14.895 --> 03:16.895
I ask for one thing
in this house!

03:16.897 --> 03:18.897
Stewie, just watch
your show upstairs.

03:18.899 --> 03:21.633
I don't want to watch it
upstairs on the small tv!

03:21.635 --> 03:24.236
I want to watch it
downstairs on the big tv!

03:24.238 --> 03:25.237
(sniffling)

03:25.239 --> 03:27.472
I want to watch my show!

03:27.474 --> 03:29.541
(crying, screaming)

03:31.744 --> 03:33.645
Oh, no, stewie's
having a tantrum.

03:33.647 --> 03:35.380
Come here, sweetie.

03:37.550 --> 03:38.584
Ow!

03:38.586 --> 03:40.018
Screw you, you little turd!

03:40.020 --> 03:41.453
(crying)

03:42.488 --> 03:44.189
What's all that noise?

03:44.191 --> 03:47.259
Aw, do you want a hug
from your big sister?

03:48.595 --> 03:49.761
Ow!

03:51.898 --> 03:54.900
You've earned yourself
a time-out, young man.

03:54.902 --> 03:57.836
Now, you stay in here
until you can behave.

03:57.838 --> 04:00.005
I hate you!
You always ruin everything!

04:00.007 --> 04:01.940
God, it's a family of idiots!

04:01.942 --> 04:03.175
I wish...

04:03.177 --> 04:05.244
I wish I was never born!

04:06.212 --> 04:07.679
Not tonight, rupert.

04:07.681 --> 04:09.581
I'm much too upset.

04:13.586 --> 04:15.020
Knock, knock.

04:15.022 --> 04:16.021
Stewie?

04:16.023 --> 04:17.623
Hey, I just
wanted to check

04:17.625 --> 04:18.857
On how you're
doing, buddy.

04:18.859 --> 04:20.626
You put on quite
a show last night.

04:20.628 --> 04:22.127
I am done with this family.

04:22.129 --> 04:23.695
They don't deserve me.
They're all just...

04:23.697 --> 04:24.963
Oh, you dick,
you just came in

04:24.965 --> 04:26.098
To charge your phone.

04:26.100 --> 04:28.267
Sorry, peter's using
all the outlets.

04:29.736 --> 04:31.436
Toast house.

04:31.438 --> 04:34.039
Whatever. I'm gonna be
out of this place soon anyway.

04:34.041 --> 04:35.540
What, are you
running away from home?

04:35.542 --> 04:36.608
Better.

04:39.445 --> 04:40.579
What the hell?

04:40.581 --> 04:42.781
You rebuilt
your time machine?

04:42.783 --> 04:45.083
I thought you
swore off time travel,

04:45.085 --> 04:46.952
'cause you couldn't stop
yourself from altering the past.

04:46.954 --> 04:48.420
Look, brian,
I need this machine

04:48.422 --> 04:49.921
To alter the past
for the better.

04:49.923 --> 04:50.922
What do you mean?

04:50.924 --> 04:52.658
I loathe this family.

04:52.660 --> 04:55.594
Being born into it was clearly
some sort of cosmic mistake,

04:55.596 --> 04:58.330
So I'm going back in time
to prevent that mistake.

04:58.332 --> 05:00.766
I'm going to break up lois
and the fat man

05:00.768 --> 05:02.501
Before they can conceive me.

05:02.503 --> 05:03.969
Stewie, it's one tv show.

05:03.971 --> 05:05.170
You're overreacting.

05:05.172 --> 05:07.105
It's not just the
tv show, brian.

05:07.107 --> 05:08.674
I'm tired of
living with morons.

05:08.676 --> 05:11.810
Remember when I tried to open
that lemonade stand with chris?

05:11.812 --> 05:13.612
All right,
that'll be ten cents.

05:13.614 --> 05:14.680
Chris, pour the man
his lemonade.

05:14.682 --> 05:15.981
Chris:
I can't!

05:15.983 --> 05:18.750
The lemonade tricked me
and got away!

05:18.752 --> 05:21.753
Lemons are god's children!

05:21.755 --> 05:23.655
And the fat man
won't even let me

05:23.657 --> 05:25.324
Celebrate a
proper birthday.

05:25.326 --> 05:27.359
Happy birthday, stewie!

05:27.361 --> 05:29.861
And here's your
equal-attention cake, peter.

05:29.863 --> 05:31.229
Yay!

05:31.998 --> 05:32.998
Oh, come on!

05:33.000 --> 05:34.700
Yay! Double wishes!

05:36.202 --> 05:37.202
One...

05:41.307 --> 05:42.541
...Two.

05:42.543 --> 05:44.609
And meg's the
biggest pig of all.

05:44.611 --> 05:45.610
Meg:
Great.

05:45.612 --> 05:47.813
The string broke again.

05:47.815 --> 05:51.149
Hey, there, tiny hands.

05:51.151 --> 05:53.151
Look, stewie, I know
you're angry about last night,

05:53.153 --> 05:55.220
But you're talking about
erasing your existence.

05:55.222 --> 05:56.388
That's crazy.

05:56.390 --> 05:59.124
("barracuda" ringtone plays)

05:59.126 --> 06:01.793
Whose ringtone
is "barracuda"?

06:01.795 --> 06:04.029
Oh, god,
that's frumpy ann.

06:04.031 --> 06:05.497
Frumpy ann
does everything.

06:05.499 --> 06:06.998
Look, I-I got to
get this call,

06:07.000 --> 06:09.000
But don't do
anything stupid.

06:09.002 --> 06:10.969
Yo, girl,
how you livin'?

06:10.971 --> 06:12.437
Ugh.

06:14.574 --> 06:17.542
All right, rupert,
prepare to time travel.

06:17.544 --> 06:19.578
Oh, and by the way,
thanks for asking me

06:19.580 --> 06:22.080
If I wanted something
from subway, too.

06:41.367 --> 06:42.534
Where am I?

06:42.536 --> 06:45.404
This looks like my room,
but something's off.

06:45.406 --> 06:47.372
Oh, that's right,
this isn't my room yet.

06:47.374 --> 06:49.107
Wonder what
they're using it for.

06:51.411 --> 06:54.179
Oh, my god, he had
a public access show?

06:54.181 --> 06:56.681
Live from the shores
of rhode island,

06:56.683 --> 06:58.583
It's the fatty
who drives you batty!

06:58.585 --> 07:00.585
Peter griffin!

07:00.587 --> 07:02.754
(applause)

07:04.223 --> 07:05.724
Hey, hey, hey, douche bags!

07:05.726 --> 07:07.692
We got a great show
for you tonight.

07:07.694 --> 07:09.728
Karen washington from
the rhode island zoo

07:09.730 --> 07:12.063
And some rejected toys
you're not gonna believe.

07:12.065 --> 07:13.965
So stick around, or...

07:13.967 --> 07:17.369
Studio audience:
I'll come to your house
and murder you!

07:17.371 --> 07:19.838
I wonder what else is different.

07:21.140 --> 07:23.041
♪ lucky there's a man who ♪

07:23.043 --> 07:24.709
♪ positively can do ♪

07:24.711 --> 07:26.244
♪ all the things that make us ♪

07:26.246 --> 07:28.480
♪ la la la... ♪

07:28.482 --> 07:31.650
She is camel toe-ing
the hell out of that leotard.

07:39.592 --> 07:42.627
All right, rupert, time to
break up lois and the fat man

07:42.629 --> 07:45.330
Before they can conceive me
by pressing butts together.

07:45.332 --> 07:47.065
Well, you don't know, either!

07:48.734 --> 07:51.336
Hey, lois, I drawed
you a picture.

07:53.172 --> 07:55.307
It's me and you
on the space moon,

07:55.309 --> 07:57.642
'cause I would
love you anywhere.

07:57.644 --> 08:00.745
Oh, peter.
I'd love you anywhere, too.

08:02.482 --> 08:04.983
Wow, peter and lois
were really in love

08:04.985 --> 08:06.518
Before I was born.

08:06.520 --> 08:08.687
And this is me getting
you from behind,

08:08.689 --> 08:11.256
'cause in space no one
can hear you scream.

08:11.258 --> 08:13.425
(laughs):
Oh, peter!

08:13.427 --> 08:16.528
Breaking them up may prove to be
more difficult than I thought.

08:16.530 --> 08:18.663
Though I've faced
bigger challenges before.

08:18.665 --> 08:21.266
<i>Like when I had to ride
that bike in the muppet movie.</i>

08:21.268 --> 08:23.101
(folksy music plays)

08:23.103 --> 08:24.102
That's right.

08:24.104 --> 08:26.271
Stewie long legs
just blew your mind.

08:29.342 --> 08:31.843
All right, rupert,
now to break up my parents.

08:31.845 --> 08:34.613
The number one thing
couples fight about is money.

08:34.615 --> 08:36.715
So I've maxed out
lois's credit card

08:36.717 --> 08:38.783
On vibrating marital aids.

08:41.654 --> 08:43.788
Peter, there's an open box
in the kitchen

08:43.790 --> 08:45.657
Addressed to me
with nothing inside.

08:45.659 --> 08:48.226
(vibrating): Uh, yeah, when I
opened it up, it was empty.

08:48.228 --> 08:49.828
Well, that's
very strange,

08:49.830 --> 08:52.364
Because it looked large
enough to hold many items.

08:52.366 --> 08:53.365
(doorbell rings)

08:53.367 --> 08:54.533
(vibrating):
It's the mailman!

08:54.535 --> 08:55.534
I'll get it!

08:55.536 --> 08:57.369
No! Me!
I'll get it!

08:57.371 --> 08:59.137
(vibrating):
Huh. Maybe I had more in common

08:59.139 --> 09:01.106
With this family than I thought.

09:12.919 --> 09:14.219
Oh, my god, peter!

09:14.221 --> 09:15.687
What happened
to your hair?

09:15.689 --> 09:16.721
I don't know. I...

09:16.723 --> 09:18.189
I'm bald!

09:18.191 --> 09:19.224
You did this!

09:19.226 --> 09:20.825
What the hell's
the matter with you?!

09:20.827 --> 09:23.762
I didn't do it, but...
But you look really cool.

09:23.764 --> 09:24.829
I do?

09:24.831 --> 09:27.933
Yeah, you look like you
could be a celebrity.

09:28.868 --> 09:30.869
Hey, can I get
your autograph?

09:30.871 --> 09:32.938
Oh, of course,
here you go.

09:34.440 --> 09:36.241
They think
I'm bruce willis.

09:36.243 --> 09:38.843
<i>That was the monster
from goonies!</i>

09:43.249 --> 09:44.916
None of my attempts
to break them up

09:44.918 --> 09:47.686
Has worked thus far,
so I had to up our game.

09:47.688 --> 09:49.955
Lois, what the hell did you do?!

09:49.957 --> 09:51.623
I just got a note from goodwill

09:51.625 --> 09:53.525
Thanking me for
donating all my porn.

09:53.527 --> 09:54.526
What?!

09:54.528 --> 09:56.127
I'm sick and tired
of you blaming me

09:56.129 --> 09:57.562
For things I didn't do!

09:57.564 --> 09:59.564
And I've got a bone
to pick with you!

09:59.566 --> 10:01.433
I don't appreciate
how you spray-painted

10:01.435 --> 10:03.234
"vile woman"
on the bedroom wall.

10:03.236 --> 10:04.235
That wasn't me!

10:04.237 --> 10:05.570
Must've been
one of the kids!

10:05.572 --> 10:07.105
That's ridiculous,
peter!

10:07.107 --> 10:08.540
Chris can't write,

10:08.542 --> 10:10.508
And we don't allow
meg upstairs!

10:12.111 --> 10:13.745
Well, you know something,
I'm starting to think

10:13.747 --> 10:15.146
Whoever wrote
that is right!

10:15.148 --> 10:16.982
Well, maybe I don't want
to live with someone

10:16.984 --> 10:18.283
Who doesn't respect me!

10:18.285 --> 10:20.085
Well, then maybe
I should just leave!

10:20.087 --> 10:21.720
And where are you gonna go?

10:21.722 --> 10:23.788
You got nothing else
and nobody else!

10:23.790 --> 10:25.724
And now for the closer.

10:27.259 --> 10:28.727
(honks)

10:29.762 --> 10:31.830
I might go west.

10:34.567 --> 10:36.635
My god, I've done it, rupert!

10:36.637 --> 10:37.969
They've broken up!

10:37.971 --> 10:39.638
(gasps) look!

10:39.640 --> 10:40.739
It's working.

10:40.741 --> 10:42.574
I'm fading away!

10:42.576 --> 10:45.176
Well, rupert, this means
you and I will never have met.

10:45.178 --> 10:47.512
So I've got
to tell you one thing:

10:47.514 --> 10:49.814
You know that song I wrote you
for valentine's day?

10:49.816 --> 10:51.683
It's an eric carmen song.

10:51.685 --> 10:53.351
I completely ripped it off.

10:53.353 --> 10:55.420
Ah. Ah, now I feel better.

10:58.591 --> 10:59.958
(stewie groans)

10:59.960 --> 11:01.660
<i>Stewie:
Wha...</i>

11:01.662 --> 11:02.927
<i>What the devil?</i>

11:02.929 --> 11:03.928
<i>What's going on?</i>

11:03.930 --> 11:05.530
<i>Where am I?</i>

11:05.532 --> 11:06.765
Doctor:
It's a boy!

11:06.767 --> 11:09.100
<i>Stewie:
I'm in a hospital.</i>

11:09.102 --> 11:11.302
<i>My soul must have
found another carrier.</i>

11:11.304 --> 11:13.171
<i>I've been reborn!</i>

11:13.173 --> 11:15.507
(british accent):
Welcome to the world, baby chap.

11:15.509 --> 11:16.508
(gasps)

11:16.510 --> 11:17.776
I'm british?

11:17.778 --> 11:20.779
Ooh, I wonder if
I'll have one of those

11:20.781 --> 11:23.748
Pug-nosed british dogs
that licks its own snot all day.

11:25.818 --> 11:27.385
Ew, that's gross.

11:27.387 --> 11:29.354
(cockney accent):
Piss off, you little wanker.

11:29.356 --> 11:31.890
I'm not gonna be the dog
to some poof baby.

11:45.504 --> 11:47.172
Well, lad,
welcome to your home.

11:50.743 --> 11:53.411
Well, this is more like it.

11:53.413 --> 11:55.714
This is your valet,
your gardener,

11:55.716 --> 11:58.550
Your cook, your gamekeeper,
your butler, your housekeeper,

11:58.552 --> 12:00.085
Your parlor maid,
your housemaid,

12:00.087 --> 12:02.554
Your scullery maid,
your shoe de-graveler

12:02.556 --> 12:04.389
And one superfluous employee

12:04.391 --> 12:06.591
Who I am not in a gay
relationship with.

12:06.593 --> 12:08.760
Sir, we have a meeting
in the broom shed.

12:08.762 --> 12:11.663
I will now hand you
over to your mother.

12:11.665 --> 12:13.498
This will be our
last physical contact

12:13.500 --> 12:15.333
Until I give you
a firm handshake

12:15.335 --> 12:17.435
On your 18th birthday.

12:20.072 --> 12:22.774
My god, this is everything
I've ever wanted.

12:22.776 --> 12:25.710
And let's be honest, if I had
stayed with the griffins,

12:25.712 --> 12:28.213
I would have ended up like
rick springfield today.

12:28.215 --> 12:32.050
♪ I wish that
I had jesse's job. ♪

12:32.052 --> 12:33.651
(sighs)

12:37.723 --> 12:39.457
Sir, it's 6:00 p.M.

12:39.459 --> 12:42.794
And you're still in
your 5:45 tuxedo.

12:42.796 --> 12:45.263
Nigel, yesterday
I saw you smile.

12:45.265 --> 12:47.799
Is that something I need
to bring up with my father?

12:47.801 --> 12:50.802
I was just imagining
my own death, sir.

12:50.804 --> 12:52.270
You're a good man, nigel.

12:52.272 --> 12:53.872
May I pull on
your nose hair?

12:53.874 --> 12:55.740
Of course, sir.

12:55.742 --> 12:57.809
(laughing)

13:04.917 --> 13:07.485
My heavens, my father
is the commander

13:07.487 --> 13:09.587
Of the most excellent order
of the british empire,

13:09.589 --> 13:11.623
Dean of physics at oxford,

13:11.625 --> 13:14.592
And he was pre-approved for
a capital one no-hassle card.

13:14.594 --> 13:16.594
Oh, okay, so he's just
framing everything.

13:16.596 --> 13:20.131
Stewart, these are
your brothers, jaden and aidan.

13:20.133 --> 13:22.567
Jaden was first form
in his sixth levels

13:22.569 --> 13:25.436
And he's chief scrum-flanker
on his varsity boogling team,

13:25.438 --> 13:27.939
Which, as far as we know,
makes us terribly proud.

13:27.941 --> 13:30.575
Finally, siblings
who are doing stuff.

13:30.577 --> 13:32.577
I'm really happy
to meet you guys.

13:32.579 --> 13:34.245
You were an accident.

13:34.247 --> 13:36.481
You're only here because
father is a heavy sleeper

13:36.483 --> 13:38.583
With a frequent
morning stem.

13:38.585 --> 13:41.319
Okay. Aidan's the ball-breaker,
huh, jaden?

13:41.321 --> 13:45.123
Father, is "it" going
to live here for a while?

13:45.125 --> 13:46.958
Oh, aidan is the nice one.

13:46.960 --> 13:49.761
Well, if it's verbal jousting
skills you're looking for,

13:49.763 --> 13:53.665
I'm not afraid to take a little
walk on the oscar wilde side.

13:53.667 --> 13:55.700
You are a poopy head.

13:55.702 --> 13:57.936
And you... Shut up.

13:57.938 --> 14:00.104
Stewart, I think
your mouth is better

14:00.106 --> 14:02.540
At taking things in
than spewing them out.

14:02.542 --> 14:04.876
(both laughing)

14:04.878 --> 14:07.946
Wow, these guys are a little
sharper than my old family.

14:07.948 --> 14:11.115
I still remember
our duck duck goose disaster.

14:11.117 --> 14:12.317
Duck.

14:12.319 --> 14:13.318
Duck.

14:13.320 --> 14:14.319
Duck.

14:14.321 --> 14:16.321
Duck.

14:16.323 --> 14:19.457
Duck. Duck.

14:19.459 --> 14:20.725
Duck.

14:20.727 --> 14:22.227
Duck. Duck.

14:22.229 --> 14:23.294
Duck.

14:25.664 --> 14:26.664
Duck.

14:26.666 --> 14:28.533
Duck. Duck.

14:28.535 --> 14:29.901
Duck.

14:29.903 --> 14:31.703
Duck.

14:36.642 --> 14:38.376
Duck.

14:38.378 --> 14:40.879
<i>What is that other word?</i>

14:43.849 --> 14:45.483
(stewie suckling)

14:45.485 --> 14:47.252
(cockney accent):
There we are.

14:47.254 --> 14:49.554
Sorry I couldn't squeeze
no more juice outta me nippers.

14:49.556 --> 14:51.189
Oh, that's all right.

14:51.191 --> 14:54.158
I can't be mad at someone who
lost seven sons in the war.

14:54.160 --> 14:56.995
All right, my little lord,
it's time for bed.

14:56.997 --> 14:58.596
Why isn't mommy
tucking me in?

14:58.598 --> 15:00.732
Oh, hush, love,
you're born now.

15:00.734 --> 15:03.434
That's the end of all
this "mommy" nonsense.

15:06.405 --> 15:08.473
(wind howling)

15:11.043 --> 15:12.377
What the hell?

15:12.379 --> 15:14.445
I don't even get
a stuffed animal to hug?

15:14.447 --> 15:15.780
The only thing in this crib

15:15.782 --> 15:17.615
Is a 19th-century
dueling pistol.

15:17.617 --> 15:18.616
(screams)

15:18.618 --> 15:20.118
It's loaded?!

15:20.120 --> 15:22.620
British nobleman: Who dares to
shoot the bow tie off my cat?

15:22.622 --> 15:24.022
We duel at dawn!

15:24.024 --> 15:25.423
I'm just a baby!

15:25.425 --> 15:26.758
So am I!

15:26.760 --> 15:28.760
Good lord, what have I done?

15:28.762 --> 15:30.561
I don't like it here at all!

15:30.563 --> 15:31.596
I miss my family!

15:31.598 --> 15:33.865
My dumb family!

15:33.867 --> 15:35.066
Dear god.

15:35.068 --> 15:37.602
I wanted to be free
of the family of morons

15:37.604 --> 15:40.905
I was born into,
but now I'm the moron!

15:40.907 --> 15:42.573
Sir, I heard
whimpering.

15:42.575 --> 15:44.709
Shall I fetch
your crying tuxedo?

15:44.711 --> 15:46.811
No! I don't want
any more tuxedos!

15:46.813 --> 15:48.813
And I don't want a cold mother

15:48.815 --> 15:50.648
Or an oxford physics
professor father.

15:50.650 --> 15:51.649
(gasps)

15:51.651 --> 15:52.817
Wait a minute! That's it!

15:52.819 --> 15:54.619
The oxford physics lab will have

15:54.621 --> 15:56.654
Everything I need
to build a time machine.

15:56.656 --> 15:58.723
Then I can go
back to my old life!

16:00.726 --> 16:02.727
Ah, ah!
Stone floor, too cold.

16:02.729 --> 16:04.796
I'll go in the morning.

16:11.270 --> 16:14.238
Let's see, I need plutonium
for the time machine.

16:14.240 --> 16:16.240
But how do I get
past those guards?

16:16.242 --> 16:18.576
Oh, wait, that's right.
I'm in England.

16:18.578 --> 16:21.179
I can just walk past them
holding a cup of tea.

16:21.181 --> 16:22.580
Morning.
Morning.

16:22.582 --> 16:24.182
Morning.
Morning.

16:27.686 --> 16:28.619
Morning.
Morning.

16:28.621 --> 16:30.621
Morning.
Morning.

16:30.623 --> 16:33.858
Did you see something
suspicious about that baby?

16:33.860 --> 16:35.526
Well, I did at first,

16:35.528 --> 16:38.196
But then he's got the tea
vouching for him, doesn't he?

16:41.633 --> 16:43.935
(plutonium humming)

16:51.343 --> 16:52.677
Almost there.

16:52.679 --> 16:53.945
Just a few more adjustments.

16:53.947 --> 16:55.346
British father:
Stewart!
(gasps)

16:55.348 --> 16:56.781
What are you doing?

17:04.690 --> 17:06.391
All right, rupert,
I left the fat man's

17:06.393 --> 17:07.692
Entire porn collection

17:07.694 --> 17:09.794
On the curb
for goodwill to pick up.

17:10.896 --> 17:13.698
(screams)

17:17.836 --> 17:19.704
(gasps)
who the devil are you?

17:19.706 --> 17:21.005
I'm british stewie.

17:21.007 --> 17:22.573
I don't hear
anything different.

17:22.575 --> 17:23.574
I sound the same,

17:23.576 --> 17:25.176
But I spell some words
very differently.

17:25.178 --> 17:26.511
Let me write
the word "color"

17:26.513 --> 17:28.079
On a piece of
paper for you.

17:28.081 --> 17:29.480
(gasps)

17:29.482 --> 17:31.082
<i>Dear god! You are british!</i>

17:31.084 --> 17:32.250
Listen to me.

17:32.252 --> 17:33.918
You successfully prevented
your own birth,

17:33.920 --> 17:36.387
And instead you were born
into an alternate family.

17:36.389 --> 17:37.588
But you must believe me,

17:37.590 --> 17:39.824
The griffins are
your true destiny.

17:39.826 --> 17:41.659
No, they're not. They're morons.

17:41.661 --> 17:44.562
But they're your morons,
and they care about you.

17:44.564 --> 17:46.564
Besides, you shine
among these dullards.

17:46.566 --> 17:48.699
Like bob weir in
the grateful dead.

17:48.701 --> 17:50.701
That joke's for
one of our crew guys, matty.

17:50.703 --> 17:53.604
He loves the dead and he's,
uh... He's not doing so well.

17:53.606 --> 17:56.107
We love ya, captain trips.
Hang in, bro.

17:56.109 --> 17:59.610
Well, I do like being
better than everyone else.

17:59.612 --> 18:01.579
Lois: Peter, I had
nothing to do

18:01.581 --> 18:03.047
With donating
your stupid porn!

18:03.049 --> 18:04.949
If what you're
telling me is true,

18:04.951 --> 18:06.584
We can't let
them separate.

18:06.586 --> 18:08.252
If peter leaves,
I'll be unborn!

18:08.254 --> 18:09.587
Well, she's not
gonna stop him.

18:09.589 --> 18:10.755
She's furious.
(gasps)

18:10.757 --> 18:12.590
You're right!
And if I know her,

18:12.592 --> 18:13.758
She'll be heading
to the fridge

18:13.760 --> 18:15.693
For her angry
afternoon chardonnay.

18:15.695 --> 18:17.261
I've got an idea!

18:21.934 --> 18:23.768
Okay, there it is.

18:23.770 --> 18:25.436
Noon.

18:36.648 --> 18:38.549
Oh, no! He's leaving!

18:38.551 --> 18:41.152
I'm... I'm fading away!

18:41.154 --> 18:42.320
Peter, wait!

18:42.322 --> 18:44.555
What? You want to yell
at me some more?

18:44.557 --> 18:46.891
No, I want to
tell you I'm sorry.

18:46.893 --> 18:48.826
I... I don't want
you to leave.

18:48.828 --> 18:51.129
Why should I stay if
you don't even trust me?

18:51.131 --> 18:53.231
I do trust you, peter.

18:53.233 --> 18:55.566
I don't know what's
gotten into us lately.

18:55.568 --> 18:58.736
The important thing is,
we're meant to be together.

18:58.738 --> 19:00.972
I love you, peter.

19:00.974 --> 19:04.208
Aw, I love you, too, lois.

19:08.647 --> 19:10.181
I'm glad we're
staying together.

19:10.183 --> 19:12.617
Honestly, I-I don't know
what I would do on my own.

19:12.619 --> 19:15.987
Like, I literally have no
idea where food comes from.

19:15.989 --> 19:17.488
I-is it that guy?

19:17.490 --> 19:19.223
Is he the food man?

19:22.661 --> 19:25.096
No, peter, it's not him.

19:25.098 --> 19:26.297
They're making up!

19:26.299 --> 19:27.365
It's working!

19:27.367 --> 19:29.500
That means soon
you will not exist.

19:29.502 --> 19:32.670
Then I guess this
is good-bye, stewie.

19:32.672 --> 19:33.971
I'll miss you.

19:33.973 --> 19:35.439
You've taught
me so much.

19:35.441 --> 19:36.641
And you've been
a good friend.

19:36.643 --> 19:37.808
And you as well.

19:37.810 --> 19:38.976
Ah! Damn it!

19:38.978 --> 19:40.545
Help me, stewie!
Lift it off!

19:40.547 --> 19:42.313
Eh, that looks
really heavy.

19:42.315 --> 19:44.315
It is! And it's
incredibly painful!

19:44.317 --> 19:45.316
Please, help!

19:45.318 --> 19:46.617
You know,
you'll be fading away

19:46.619 --> 19:48.452
Any moment, you know?

19:48.454 --> 19:50.555
It'd be a lot of effort
ultimately for nothing.

19:50.557 --> 19:51.889
I'm choking on
my own blood!

19:51.891 --> 19:52.890
(gurgles)

19:52.892 --> 19:54.792
Call someone! Please!

19:54.794 --> 19:57.528
Well, again,
it was great knowing you.

19:57.530 --> 19:59.297
Ah! You bastard!

19:59.299 --> 20:00.698
You'll burn in hell...

20:02.234 --> 20:03.701
Ugh, finally.

20:03.703 --> 20:05.102
That was an ordeal.

20:12.644 --> 20:14.045
I... I did it!

20:14.047 --> 20:15.546
I'm back.

20:15.548 --> 20:16.714
Aw, damn it.

20:16.716 --> 20:18.649
I left my chapstick in the past.

20:19.985 --> 20:21.319
Chapstick!

20:21.321 --> 20:23.754
With smooth lips,
I will finally be able

20:23.756 --> 20:26.724
To be a mayor who kisses babies
with confidence!

20:26.726 --> 20:28.693
Hey, cracked lips!

20:28.695 --> 20:29.694
You'll see!

20:29.696 --> 20:31.762
You'll all see!

20:37.269 --> 20:39.604
Ooh, scrambled eggs!
How delightful.

20:39.606 --> 20:40.771
Thank you, lois.

20:40.773 --> 20:42.573
Well, you're certainly
in a better mood

20:42.575 --> 20:43.774
Since last
night's tantrum.

20:43.776 --> 20:46.877
You know, brian, I've realized
this is where I belong.

20:46.879 --> 20:49.714
For better or worse,
I'm a griffin.

20:49.716 --> 20:50.615
(door crashes)

20:50.617 --> 20:53.251
Coward!
I have found you!

20:53.253 --> 20:54.552
Ah!

20:54.554 --> 20:55.686
Well, it took
three years,

20:55.688 --> 20:57.688
But I am finally
through all that porn.

20:57.690 --> 21:59.123
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru